<title>FRANCE: French seize cocaine in shampoo, rum bottles.</title>
<headline>French seize cocaine in shampoo, rum bottles.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>French customs said on Thursday they had seized cocaine concealed in rum and shampoo bottles and detained three suspected smugglers in two French overseas territories.</p>
<p>Two Surinamese were held in French Guiana as they were leaving for Paris last week carrying six bottles of rum containing 4.4 kilos (9.7 lbs) of diluted cocaine.</p>
<p>A Briton was detained on the Caribbean island of Martinique after he flew in from Barbados with 7.5 kilos (16.5 lb) of the drug in shampoo bottles.</p>
</text>
